{"body":{"asks":"Whatever is mounted in a slot is agnostic and decoupled, and implements no chrome; chrome is apart from accessibility. The parent giving the card and background, a component being its content, seemed to the author smart and sane, though nesting troubles it, as a collation nests; perhaps some drawing at each slot's level. Each component library ships its own style, ours cards, another borders, the chassis caring for none: a wrapper component presenting its slot and drawing around it, perhaps reaching every slot beneath a reader as an offer, everything wrapped with some wrappers drawing nothing, or wrapping toggled; what toggling does to the tree is unexplored. A focus ring and a selection are chrome too, as OpenLight's reader gave collation selections their colours. Hosts today are display: contents and carry no box. The author does not know yet whether chrome can wait, it being connected with everything.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC004"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00E","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Chrome around nested components"}
{"body":{"asks":"Arrow keys and Enter in the completion menu, left and right across cards, perhaps / to search the actions at hand rather than the page: all just working, not, he thinks, each component's to implement. The web's native accessibility may be kept, since it is what grades a site, the chassis writing the ARIA fields from what the field says of each component. Whether ARIA suffices for every layout, a node view among them, or simpler, more powerful data is needed, is open.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC006"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00G","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Accessibility and keys defined by the system"}
{"body":{"asks":"io.propose names what it changes by its index among what a component was given, where glass matches inputs as a set, by type. And the chassis records a component drawn by a plain io.draw at its parent's place, so its propose would change its parent's argument: the chassis does not behave properly, whatever is drawn being its own in the hierarchy. Propose bound to what one was given may not be right either, once permissions let one propose what one is permitted to: perhaps propose takes a change, written first class: the thread Commits written in the field.","raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC007"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00H","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Propose by type, not position"}
{"body":{"asks":"A component in code that draws a holon in its own markup, as Value a card and prose a link, hides it from the chassis, which knows only that Value drew there; the inspector reads attributes the components set to find it. Layout as data has no such gap, and leaf components being code makes sense. The author: any io.draw should contribute to the hierarchy, so it is the chassis's to keep, not code's to project; rows and the like should be components; a table its own kit, table, row and cell, since cells align, each clickable as a component of its own. Where code draws without io.draw is not yet worth reaching.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC008"}],"stands":"leaning"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00J","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Holons drawn inside components in code"}
{"body":{"asks":"A change as a value the language can write, with its target, so that it can be drafted, verified by judging without landing, and projected, read as if landed, a branch seen before it exists; a read already carries holons not yet stored. propose would take such a change, composed by a component, rather than a replacement for what it was given, the way back one way of working one out; later judged under permissions like any commit. The author: \"we're onto something there\".","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M89280APGY7000"}],"stands":"leaning"},"id":"1M89280APGY7007","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Commits written in the field"}
{"body":{"asks":"Between a function and a program: an action that only makes a pure change upon the field, as going back in the history, needs no runtime and has no side effect but its commit, so is no program; it is an expression giving a change with its target, as back is a change to the at of @location:history, which the location already takes. Or the integration provides it. The UI has no menu actions yet; back is the first real one. Not needed yet.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M89280APGY7001"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M89280APGY7008","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Actions as changes written as expressions"}
{"body":{"asks":"Completion is wanted in various kinds of input, driven over the buffer typed into and over the whole field it completes against. If it must be defined at the root and linked to the reader, the reader is not whole and two sources must be managed; would another reader need the same? There has to be a simple, pure and honourable way. The session offered completion as data in Search's layout, shown in the overlay layer while the buffer has text; the author does not yet trust the approach.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M89280APGY7002"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M89280APGY7009","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Completion as a modality"}
{"body":{"asks":"What stands in an overlay is held by its owner in the holarchy, as the completion menu by the input, living and dying with it, its keys and way back its owner's, and only painted in the overlay layer: a portal. Whether a component draws it programmatically or it is written as data, a layer a key on the use as offer is, the author does not know. The context menu is the root's.","raised":[{"$ref":"1M89280APGY7003"}],"stands":"leaning"},"id":"1M89280APGY700A","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Overlays owned, painted in a layer"}
{"body":{"asks":"Choosing which component draws a place modifies the holarchy itself, a WYSIWYG modification and not an action; io.pick, given to components, was never asked for and is premature, and should not exist. Value's cards, rows and table modes, kept in the browser's storage, are the same choosing made by hand. Of a piece with the thread The interface open by nesting and choice.","raised":[{"$ref":"1M89280APGY7004"}],"stands":"leaning"},"id":"1M89280APGY700B","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Choosing a component edits the holarchy"}
{"body":{"asks":"Perhaps the inspector is a layer of its own: what one hovers outlined, with some information around it, and an overlay telling more; it builds on wrapping and on layers, and may be too far yet.","raised":[{"$ref":"1M89280APGY7005"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M89280APGY700C","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"The inspector as a layer"}
{"body":{"asks":"If typing in the expression bar is too laggy, the work cannot proceed so: it must be resolved, though after the first things. One read for a turn makes the engine's read longer, and separate reads and subscriptions would make each smaller; but each kept read stands on every store, so a buffer moving on a keystroke runs all again. With commits tracking where a holon exists, everything brought into another store shipped with where it came from, a read could stand only on the stores that can hold what it read: the threads Where a holon is kept and Holding links to history. Not what was tried before (21/87, 21/93).","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M89280APGY7006"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M89280APGY700D","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Typing kept fast"}